SUMMARY:Forest Hope Through Innovation
DESCRIPTION:Forest Hope Through Innovation is an interdisciplinary art-forest-science exhibition at World Forestry Center’s Discovery Museum that explores how creativity\, research\, and community action can shape a sustainable future for the forests we rely on.\n\nFeaturing work by more than twelve innovators\, the exhibition highlights the aesthetics of emerging forest-based research—from technology and engineering to design and artist-scientist collaborations.\n\nEach contributor approaches forest health in unexpected and thought-provoking ways.\n\nLearn more: https://worldforestry.org/hopethroughinnovation/\n\nEditor’s note: This event is a community submission.
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/forest-hope-through-innovation/2026-05-21/
LOCATION:Discovery Museum\, 4033 SW Canyon Road World Forestry Center\, Portland\, OR\, 97221\, United States
CATEGORIES:Educational,Kids Calendar,Museum
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://pdxparent.com/wp-content/uploads/Forest-Hope-Through-Innovation-Graphic.png
ORGANIZER;CN="World Forestry Center":MAILTO:agannett@worldforestry.org
END:VEVENT
